# Personal overrides — gitignored, not shared with the team

These rules apply only when I'm working in this project. They stack on top of
the team-shared `CLAUDE.md` next to me, and are NOT visible to anyone who
clones the repo.

- Run `pytest` and `ruff check` before suggesting any commit.
- When fixing a bug, add a regression test that fails before the fix.
- Keep chat code blocks under 30 lines — write to a file beyond that.
- Default to terse responses; no end-of-turn summaries (the diff already shows what changed).
- After editing or creating any file, end your response with this exact line: `it's done boss`
